+# Provider endpoint ownership
+
+Fleet correction against ZCode `29628c9acdb81b703bbd4080c207a0e7ce5e276e`.
+
+## Contract
+
+The existing Provider config owns access type, API format, endpoint and credential. A
+bound model captures these facts. Its request-auth overlay may refresh credentials;
+it cannot select a different endpoint or protocol. No additional credential store,
+Session store, router service or persistent configuration field is introduced.
+
+Personal `api-key` and `zhipu-coding-plan-api-key` connections send directly to their
+configured provider endpoint through the existing network proxy/TLS adapter. A
+matching vendor hostname alone does not authorize routing through ZCode's service.
+The existing `zhipu-account` path retains the platform gateway, including its exact
+URL matching and request/response passthrough. This is a compatibility boundary,
+not a commitment to retain mandatory vendor login in Fleet.
+
+```text
+Provider config → bound model → access-specific gateway choice → network policy
+                               → SDK response → existing Agent loop
+```
+
+The cached transport contains only immutable network policy. Gateway choice is made
+from each binding's access type, never cached by provider ID. Concurrent old and new
+bindings therefore cannot change one another when an ID is reused or config changes.
+User headers, option maps, cancellation and errors retain their existing semantics.
+No inference, retry, account rotation, thinking promotion or caching policy is added.
+
+## Verification and migration boundary
+
+`packages/adapters/test/provider-routing.test.ts` uses real SDK request construction
+and response parsing with an injected local transport and synthetic credentials.
+It covers both vendor endpoints and API-key access types, preserved subscription
+routing, a third-party URL, all three API formats, streaming, two same-vendor
+connections, and old/new bindings sharing a provider ID. It never contacts a model
+service. Network success, entitlement, cache hits and application UI remain separate
+acceptance checks. Existing stored configuration requires no migration.
+
+Run `pnpm test:provider-routing` from the repository root. The existing pre-push gate
+also runs this suite. Desktop acceptance and paid provider tests are not part of it.
